meta {
  name: Read availability
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

get {
  url: {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}/availability
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  200. Served through Redis, and advisory - which the response says itself: calculatedAt
  stamps when the figure was taken, and canBeLoaned is a statement about a moment that has
  already passed by the time you read it.

  Nothing in the loan path consults this. Whether a copy can actually be taken is decided
  once, inside POST /loans, by an atomic conditional UPDATE against PostgreSQL. This
  endpoint is for showing a reader whether it is worth trying.

  Every write that moves the count - a loan, a return, a cancellation, a change to the total
  - drops this key immediately after its transaction commits, so run this before and after
  Loans > Lend a copy to see it refresh.
}
